Subject: Diagnostic: rollback sync test
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Rollback study. Between two fixed steps of a match, the port's sync test
(src/platform/sync_test.cpp in the game module) may save the match, run a
few steps, restore it and run them again, comparing the game's own checksum
after each step and the memory at the end. A step is exactly what
FixedUpdateTask::Run does for one: pads, inputs, then the simulation.
Without RECHARGED_SYNCTEST the hook returns at once and the game is unchanged.

Add include/mscharged_synctest.h, the sync test's interface to the port: this
hook and the switches tweak patches 0029-0031 use.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_synctest.h b/include/mscharged_synctest.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..19ce4fe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/mscharged_synctest.h
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#ifndef MSCHARGED_SYNCTEST_H
+#define MSCHARGED_SYNCTEST_H
+
+// Rollback sync test of the native port (src/platform/sync_test.cpp in the game
+// module). It does nothing unless RECHARGED_SYNCTEST is set.
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+// Between two fixed steps of a match. Every few steps the test saves the
+// match, runs `step` a few times (0: no simulation step ran, 1: one ran, -1:
+// one ran and a NIS stops the simulation), restores the match, runs them
+// again and compares `checksum` after each step and the memory at the end.
+// `task` and `taskBytes` are the fixed update task, restored with the arenas.
+void mscharged_synctest_between_steps(int (*step)(void), unsigned (*checksum)(void), void* task,
+                                      unsigned long taskBytes);
+// Around each fixed simulation step (1 at its start, 0 at its end; tweak
+// patch 0029).
+void mscharged_synctest_fixed_step(int running);
+// Whether a sound or audio effect the game asks for now must not be made:
+// during the steps of a match under the sync test, so the simulation never
+// owns audio state (tweak patches 0029 and 0031).
+bool mscharged_synctest_silences_sounds(void);
+// Whether the sync test runs: matches then use the deterministic AI clocks of
+// network games even offline (tweak patch 0030).
+bool mscharged_synctest_active(void);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif // MSCHARGED_SYNCTEST_H
+#endif // MSCHARGED_TWEAKS
